{},[33,459,460],{"href":460,"rel":461},"https://twitter.com/DrugPackagesBot",[37],[29,463,464],{},[33,465,466],{"href":466,"rel":467},"https://twitter.com/NewMythologies",[37],[29,469,470],{},[33,471,472],{"href":472,"rel":473},"https://twitter.com/numbersbot0001",[37],[29,475,476],{},[33,477,478],{"href":478,"rel":479},"https://twitter.com/numbersbot0002",[37],[29,481,482],{},[33,483,484],{"href":484,"rel":485},"http://twitter.com/KimIlSungismBot",[37],[29,487,488],{},[33,489,490],{"href":490,"rel":491},"https://twitter.com/FairyTaleTitles",[37],[29,493,494],{},[33,495,496],{"href":496,"rel":497},"https://twitter.com/NewsForGoats",[37],[29,499,500],{},[33,501,502],{"href":502,"rel":503},"https://twitter.com/BoingBoingHuffR",[37],[29,505,506],{},[33,507,510],{"href":508,"rel":509},"https://twitter.com/SolanisBot01",[37],"SolanasBot01",[29,512,513],{},[33,514,517],{"href":515,"rel":516},"https://twitter.com/SolanasBot02",[37],"SolanasBot02",[29,519,520],{},[33,521,524],{"href":522,"rel":523},"https://twitter.com/SolanasBot03",[37],"SolanasBot03",{"title":165,"searchDepth":166,"depth":166,"links":526},[527],{"id":342,"depth":166,"text":343},"2019-09-14T00:00:00.000Z","2025-12-29T00:00:00.000Z","Notes on automated bots, mostly posting to Twitter or Tumblr",{},"/blog/automated-bots",{"title":277,"description":530},{"src":535,"mime":265,"alt":536,"width":537,"height":538},"/media/sample.webp","Mountain",1200,630,"blog/automated-bots",[338,541,187,542],"automation","tumblr","3RzqzWOQhzXRlCM0y6KAd4RakK8ss7BJDycoDY_K_9E",{"id":545,"title":546,"author":8,"body":547,"date":528,"dateUpdated":170,"description":597,"excerpt":170,"extension":172,"headline":546,"meta":598,"navigation":174,"path":599,"seo":600,"socialImage":601,"stem":602,"tags":603,"__hash__":607},"blog/blog/watmap.md","WATMAP and other delights",{"type":10,"value":548,"toc":595},[549,553,559,574,583,586],[196,550,552],{"id":551},"we-can-rebuild-it-for-you-wholesale","We can rebuild it for you wholesale!",[13,554,555],{},[16,556],{"alt":557,"src":558},"My son reimagined via WATMAP","/media/watmap.00.png",[13,560,561,562,567,568,573],{},"Processing2/3 code written by ",[33,563,566],{"href":564,"rel":565},"https://github.com/tsulej/GenerateMe/tree/master/watmap",[37],"GenerateMe",". See their ",[33,569,572],{"href":570,"rel":571},"https://generateme.tumblr.com/",[37],"TumblrBlog"," for use and tips.",[13,575,576,577,582],{},"A ",[33,578,581],{"href":579,"rel":580},"http://everythingability.com/",[37],"friend"," thinks of it a \"a poor-man's GAN\". I can see the similarities: an image is \"recreated\", using elements from something else.",[13,584,585],{},"Original developer refers to it as part of a \"glitch-aesthetic\" which I get - but it's not a glitch, an error. There are seeming \"hiccups\" in the discontinuities. It's essentially a tile-mosaic replicator using a quad-tree to focus on sizes. It takes a long time to process, mainly due to the quad-tree preocessing.",[13,587,588,589,594],{},"I thought that ",[33,590,593],{"href":591,"rel":592},"https://www.instagram.com/richard.winters/",[37],"Richard Winters"," (last time I checked, all images had been removed, which makes me sad) was using a custom version inspired by WATMAP, but I've long-since changed my mind. Using square-subsections (instead of variadic-sized rectangles) and processes each color channel (RGB?) separately. So, channel-based tile-sets.",{"title":165,"searchDepth":166,"depth":166,"links":596},[],"A glitch-aesthetic mosaic image-remaker built in Processing by somebody else",{},"/blog/watmap",{"title":546,"description":597},{"src":535,"mime":265,"alt":536,"width":537,"height":538},"blog/watmap",[187,604,605,606],"processing","glitch","tools","GCus75-dbBoVYc4LsyYAqkVEKIrUKqwLZRMqoCuJBm8",1785121133768]